{"id": "EUVD-2021-34897", "enisaUuid": "044f6766-730e-33eb-801e-12dd53585011", "description": "FineReport 9.0 contains a path traversal vulnerability in the /WebReport/ReportServer design_save_svg operation that allows unauthenticated attackers to write arbitrary files via the filePath parameter. Attackers can send a POST request with directory traversal sequences in filePath and a __CONTENT__ payload to write a JSP webshell and achieve remote code execution. Exploitation evidence was first observed by the Shadowserver Foundation on 2023-10-14.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T10:57:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T10:57:29", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/NHPT/WebReportV9Exp/blob/main/WebReport_Exp.py", "https://github.com/PeiQi0/PeiQi-WIKI-Book/blob/main/docs/wiki/oa/%E5%B8%86%E8%BD%AFOA/%E5%B8%86%E8%BD%AF%E6%8A%A5%E8%A1%A8%20V9%20design_save_svg%20%E4%BB%BB%E6%84%8F%E6%96%87%E4%BB%B6%E8%A6%86%E7%9B%96%E6%96%87%E4%BB%B6%E4%B8%8A%E4%BC%A0.md", "https://github.com/projectdiscovery/nuclei-templates/blob/main/http/vulnerabilities/finereport/fine-report-v9-file-upload.yaml", "https://www.fanruan.com/en/finereport", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/finereport-9.0-unauthenticated-path-traversal-file-write-via-reportserver"], "aliases": ["CVE-2021-48014", "GHSA-wxvw-chm6-9q9h"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f9c75dc2-8235-3eaf-9092-d05cd099d092", "product": {"name": "FineReport", "vendor": {"name": "FanRuan"}}, "product_version": "9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "05a2471c-f75e-3235-9407-1632f4962af2", "vendor": {"name": "FanRuan"}}], "isExploited": false}